HAMT

Persistent maps, sets and vectors.

A persistent container is one where an update returns a new container and
leaves the one it was called on exactly as it was. The two share nearly all
of their memory, so keeping the old one costs a few small nodes and not a
copy.

Requires a C compiler and perl 5.10 or later. No runtime prerequisites.


INSTALLATION

To install this module, run the following commands:

	perl Makefile.PL
	make
	make test
	make install

SUPPORT AND DOCUMENTATION

After installing, you can find documentation for this module with the
perldoc command.

    perldoc HAMT

You can also look for information at:

    RT, CPAN's request tracker (report bugs here)
        https://rt.cpan.org/NoAuth/Bugs.html?Dist=HAMT

    Search CPAN
        https://metacpan.org/release/HAMT


